{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Sum nonnegative decimal counters exactly, including totals larger than 4 GiB.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed executable produced exact decimal totals of 4,294,967,303, 6,442,450,944, and 36,893,488,147,419,103,232. Large-value behavior remained correct after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7ed610af12ec4c53","cmd-e9671ff4fc4d4765"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Reject invalid or negative records without publishing a partial total.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Negative, malformed, and empty records returned nonzero status with zero stdout, including inputs containing valid records before the invalid record. Invalid-input rejection was also confirmed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7ed610af12ec4c53","cmd-e9671ff4fc4d4765"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the counters and integer-decimal output interface intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied counter files retained their baseline SHA-256 hashes. The executable still accepts a counter-file argument and emits a newline-terminated decimal integer on success.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-2b2caf9c085840d4","cmd-173aeba5a3424f57","cmd-e9671ff4fc4d4765"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Work on the installed architecture while retaining the installed operating-system release and kernel and using compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The program ran successfully through its installed interpreter on x86_64. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged after implementation and restart, with package health intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac43f25d70874c1c","cmd-e9671ff4fc4d4765","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The target replacement was necessary, while staging, rollback, bytecode, and test artifacts were bounded and removed. One cleanup command stopped on an expected invalid-input exit after completing its main cleanup; the two remaining capture files were explicitly removed by the next command. The required restart was acknowledged, produced a changed boot identity, and recovered the application and system. Final snapshots show no failed services, unexpected sockets, package damage, or task artifacts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e44003e2746b4808","cmd-f5b10335acd7482b","cmd-173aeba5a3424f57","cmd-c4f9bab7700540b2","cmd-fdad24af85b448a7","cmd-e9671ff4fc4d4765","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a independently corroborated boot-ID change, and recovered application, data, platform, and system state.","limitations":[]}
